@startuml sequence_growth
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
autonumber

title Feedback growth and propagation: net.addFeedback(A, B, n) when C already reads B

participant network
participant "A : dense" as A
participant "B : dense" as B
participant "C : dense" as C
participant "C's group\n(weight_matrix)" as CW

note over B, C : earlier: net.connect(B, C)\n-> C has a group reading B,\nC is a reader of B

network -> B : addNeurons(n, A)
B -> B : create n neurons (same flags and jitter)
B -> B : new Group {inputs = A's output range,\nneurons = the n new ones, sources = {A}}\nweights: one row each, drawn from the Initial stream
B -> A : readFrom(A): B becomes a reader of A (once)
B -> B : append n entries to the output buffer

B -> B : outputGrew(old size)
loop each reader of B, in registration order
  B -> C : sourceGrew(B, offset, n)
  loop each group of C whose sources include B
    C -> C : group.inputs += B's range [offset, offset + n)
    C -> CW : appendColumns(n, new weights row after row)
  end
end

network -> network : record Edge{A, B, Feedback, n}\nand BuildOp{Feedback, A, B, n}

note over C
  if C's growth also added neurons somewhere,
  its own readers would be notified in turn:
  growth cascades downstream
end note

@enduml
